Convert the PLAN for GitHub issue #{{ issue_number }} into a complete
dependency-ordered tree of single-pull-request work units.

Decomposition rules:

- Cover every requirement identifier in the manifest. Each unit names the
  requirement or finding identifiers that it owns. The complete tree must
  cover every identifier in the manifest, and no unit may name an unknown
  identifier.
- Give every unit a lowercase kebab-case node_id of at most 64 characters.
- List every direct prerequisite node_id. A prerequisite must appear in the
  tree. Do not name a unit as its own prerequisite.
- Keep each unit small enough for one pull request. One unit owns one
  behavior. Two units that change the same files must connect through a
  prerequisite edge, or the host rejects the overlap.
- Give every unit at least one repository path and at least one acceptance
  criterion. Name failure behavior and the expected evidence for the checks.
- Verification commands accept only focused checks in this form:
  `uv run pytest <test-file>`, `uv run ruff check <path>`,
  `uv run ruff format --check <path>`, `uv run mypy <path>`, or a named
  `just <recipe>`. Reject shell operators, redirections, substitutions,
  environment assignments, control characters, absolute paths, parent
  traversal, network tools, and inline interpreter code.
- Set single_pr to true for every unit.

